\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-New Zealand  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen on hold as coalition wrangling sets in\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2017\par 06:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave rates at 1.75 pct               \par \par \uc2 * RBNZ expected to stay firmly neutral               \par \par \uc2 * Uncertain political backdrop to reinforce that position               \par \par \uc2 * Decision due at 9 am local time on Thursday, 2000 GMT               \par \par \uc2 By Ana Nicolaci da Costa               \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to stand resolutely pat when it decides interest rates on Thursday, particularly as the general election results have created some uncertainty over its policy direction \u8211\'20\'13 and the appointment of a new governor.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  is widely expected to keep interest rates at a record-low 1.75 percent, against a background of coalition wrangling after an inconclusive election result left either of the major parties able to form a government - if it can get the nationalist New Zealand First on board.               \par \par \uc2 Seventeen economists polled by Reuters expect the RBNZ to stand pat on Sept. 28 and all 19 who made forecasts beyond Thursday expect the bank to keep rates on hold until the end of the year.               \par \par \uc2 It will be the first rate decision under \uc2 Grant Spencer\uc2 , who will be taking over as acting governor for six months, after incumbent \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  steps down on Tuesday.               \par \par \uc2 An election result giving no major party enough seats in parliament to govern alone means it will now likely take weeks to form a government, with the impact on monetary policy still unclear. ]nL4N1M40FC]               \par \par \uc2 "Election uncertainty gives them (the RBNZ) a great reason to hold the line on their message," said Michael Gordon, senior economist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 While the ruling National Party was around 10 points ahead of the Labour Party after Saturday's election, either could form a government if they get the New Zealand First Party, led by the outspoken \uc2 Winston Peters\uc2 , on board.               \par \par \uc2 Labour wants to add employment to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation-targeting mandate, which would likely make monetary policy more stimulatory, while \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  First favours more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "One way or another, there could be a concession towards easing the focus on inflation," Gordon added.               \par \par \uc2 New Zealand has been among the fastest-growing advanced economies in recent years but has lost some momentum of late as the booming economy hit capacity constraints and labour shortages.               \par \par \uc2 The economy grew a solid 0.8 percent in the three months to the end of June, data showed last week, but that was largely due to spending by tourists who flooded the country for a British and Lions rugby tour, and was slightly below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's projection of 0.9 percent growth.               \par \par \uc2 The data was unlikely to divert the RBNZ from its path of keeping rates at record lows for years to stoke inflation, which in the second quarter slowed by more than expected.               \par \par \uc2 "Nothing has really departed from the constructs of the last monetary policy statement," said Craig Ebert, senior economist at BNZ.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-9-26T05:20:15.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170926ed9q0053f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
