\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-NZ dollar poised for big monthly fall, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen way off\b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2017\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * NZ dollar not far from lowest level in over two months\par \par \uc2 * Falls on softening economy, political outlook\par \par \uc2 * Noise on potential \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weighs (Updates with Wheeler comments and market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Ana Nicolaci da Costa\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar is poised for its worst monthly fall since January 2016 as talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its gains adds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes, but market participants say the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  is nowhere close to acting.\par \par \uc2 Some media interviews sparked speculation this month that the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be one step closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, after Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has such powers at a parliament hearing following the latest rates decision.\par \par \uc2 Asked by Reuters at the time whether Wheeler's comments suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a bit closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , RBNZ Assistant Governor \uc2 John McDermott\uc2  said: "No... if we were designing that you would find that in the press conference, it could even be in the statement."\par \par \uc2 Historically, the RBNZ has been very reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the noise helped take the Kiwi, which has been falling since late July, down to its lowest levels over two months.\par \par \uc2 It briefly fell back towards those levels on Wednesday after Wheeler reiterated a lower New Zealand dollar was needed to increase tradables inflation and help rebalance growth, underscoring how sensitive it currently is.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely any time soon given that the Kiwi was not exceptionally high and that its level was justified by economic fundamentals - two key conditions for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act in the market.\par \par \uc2 "Given the criteria that the RBNZ sets out for themselves on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I don't think they are anywhere near \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stuart Ive, private client manager at OM Financial.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that they mentioned it was almost by an off the cuff remark obviously aimed at, to some extent, jaw-boning the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down."\par \par \uc2 At $0.7257, the New Zealand dollar is not far from its lowest levels in more than two months against the U.S. dollar. It had already traded well below over two-year highs of $0.7558 before Wheeler's comments at around $0.7337.\par \par \uc2 It looks set for a loss of 3.4 percent this month, the biggest since a 5.2 percent drop in early 2016. But it has still gained nearly 5 percent against the greenback so far this year.\par \par \uc2 A recent softening in economic data gave investors an excuse to cash in on their long positions in the New Zealand dollar, or bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rise.\par \par \uc2 Investors also pushed out rate hike bets after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck to its neutral position in August, weighing on the local dollar.\par \par \uc2 More downside is expected in the run-up to a general election in September that has become highly contested after a change in Labour leadership.\par \par \uc2 Even though first-quarter growth and second quarter inflation underwhelmed expectations, New Zealand is still expected to be among the fastest growing advanced economies this year and its terms of trade are also expected to remain solid.\par \par \uc2 The country's term of trade reached its highest level in 40 years in the first quarter of 2017 and a second-quarter release later this week is expected to show similarly upbeat data. Trade data is due on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thinking about whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is overvalued or undervalued, the RBNZ is thinking about the terms of trade," Joseph Capurso, strategist, at CBA said.\par \par \uc2 "If the terms of trade is the biggest driver of the New Zealand dollar and that's the highest ever, then it's hard to make the conclusion that the New Zealand dollar is overvalued."\par \par \uc2 On a trade-weighted basis, the New Zealand dollar this week hit its lowest in over three months at around 75.59, well off a 5-1/2-month high of 79.26 in July and far below near two-year highs of 80.13 seen in February. Analysts said this makes an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely.\par \par \uc2 "There (were) about 20 other opportunities ... during the year when it was actually a lot higher," Jason Wong, senior market strategist at BNZ said.\par \par \uc2 "No one really believes the Reserve Bank is going to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It makes no sense whatsoever."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ana Nicolaci da Costa; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-30T03:41:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170830ed8u003cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
