\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Down Late as Resistance Holds\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2014\par 07:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar is slightly lower late Friday as it struggles to break past a key resistance level.\par \par \uc2 ASB Bank Head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  institutional sales Tim Kelleher said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was struggling to break through strong resistance at US$0.8000 and this had seen some softness. He added if it failed to breach this overnight he expected to see the pair move lower over the next few days.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw significant volatility after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  re-released the Sep. 25 bank's statement earlier. A spokesman from RBNZ said the statement was old and accidentally resent this morning. The New Zealand dollar dropped to US$0.7885 from US$0.7935, although it quickly bounced back.\par \par \uc2 The statement described the level of the New Zealand dollar as unjustified and unsustainable had weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it was initially released in September as the language had been interpreted by the market as signalling potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading at US$0.7934 late Thursday in New Zealand, compared with US$0.7992 late Thursday. The New Zealand dollar was at A$0.9066 compared with A$0.9040.\par \par \uc2 The most significant event on the local calendar next week is the release of third-quarter inflation data.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast from a Wall Street Journal poll of 13 economists sees the consumer price index in 3Q up 0.5% on quarter, compared with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations of a 0.7% increase. The poll expects the index to be up 1.2% on year compared to RBNZ expectations of a 1.3%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com, @lucy_craymer\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 17, 2014 01:23 ET (05:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141017eaah000fi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
