\par\par \b \uc2 NZ  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  surplus slides on high NZ dlr, cuts dividend\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2014\par 06:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Oct 1 (Reuters) - New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a sharply lower annual profit and slashed its dividend to the government because of losses caused by the country's high exchange rate, the annual report showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBNZ), which earlier this week disclosed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push an already-weakened NZ dollar lower, reported a net profit of NZ$56 million ($43.6 million) in the year to June 30 against the previous year's NZ$308 million.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the rise in the New Zealand dollar - up 9.8 percent against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the year to June 30 - resulted in valuation losses of NZ$198 million on its unhedged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position.\par \par \uc2 It said it would pay a dividend of NZ$20 million compared with the previous year's NZ$175 million.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank considers the current level of the exchange rate to be unsustainable, particularly in light of the 41 percent decline in global dairy prices since February 2014," RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said in a statement dated Aug 21.\par \par \uc2 Last week Wheeler renewed his warning about the New Zealand dollar's 'unsustainable' level, and on Monday RBNZ data showed it had sold NZ$521 million in August, adding pressure on the falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The kiwi hit a three-year high of $0.8839 against the U.S. dollar in July, but has since touched a 14-month low of $0.7708.\par \par \uc2 In the report, Wheeler said the strong kiwi dollar has been an unhelpful headwind hurting local exporters, but lowered tradable inflation and helped to spread the benefits of elevated commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 However, he also said domestic inflation pressures needed to be watched, singling out a rise in demand pressures in the construction sector.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ raised its cash rate by a total of 100 basis points to 3.5 percent between March and July, before pausing to assess the impact of its tightening.\par \par \uc2 The economy has started to slow from the second quarter, with benign inflation pressures and softer commodity prices. The bank is seen on hold until next March at least.\par \par \uc2 ($1= NZ$1.2855) (Reporting by Gyles Beckford; Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-1T05:39:14.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141001eaa10043f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
