\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Idea: NZD/JPY Might Fall to 82.39, 81.36 in Coming Days\b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2014\par 03:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Korean (English)\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --NZD/JPY short-term technical outlook is negative\par \par \uc2 --Cross may fall to 82.39, and possibly to 81.36 in coming days\par \par \uc2 --Daily global close above 200-day moving average would abort bearish view\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Jerry Tan\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The New Zealand dollar plunged to its lowest in more than seven months against the yen Monday on data pointing to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Kiwi-negative comments from the prime minister.\par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest the Kiwi/yen cross could decline further to 82.39, and possibly to 81.36 in coming days.\par \par \uc2 The antipodean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell Monday to Y84.33, its weakest since Feb. 20, after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  revealed it sold a net NZ$521 million (US$404 million) in August, the largest reduction in New Zealand dollar assets since July 2007 and significantly more than the NZ$2 million it sold in July, suggesting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The data confirms that the RBNZ is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times when the "\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is seen as unjustified and when market conditions are ripe for a successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Westpac\uc2  economist \uc2 Michael Gordon\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment for the Kiwi was also damped Monday after Prime Minister \uc2 John Key\uc2  was reported as signaling that US$0.6500 would be a fair value for the Kiwi.\par \par \uc2 The NZD/JPY daily price chart is currently displaying a negative short-term technical picture.\par \par \uc2 The five-day moving average is below the 15-day moving average and declining.\par \par \uc2 The daily Moving Average Convergence/Divergence and slow stochastic indicators are bearish, while the rate-of-change momentum indicator is declining inside negative territory.\par \par \uc2 Rallies in spot NZD/JPY would be opportunities to accumulate shorts for a near-term fall to 82.39--the measured objective upon breach of support at the Aug. 8 low of 85.71.\par \par \uc2 An extension of the fall would target 81.36--the Feb. 4 swing low.\par \par \uc2 However, the anticipated near-term Kiwi/yen decline would be deferred on a global daily close above the 200-day moving average, now at 87.13.\par \par \uc2 At 0451 GMT Monday, the Kiwi was quoted at Y84.90 in the interbank spot NZD/JPY market.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Jerry Tan\uc2  at jerry.tan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 Jerry Tan\uc2  is a regional technical analyst for Dow Jones Newswires, Asia Pacific. He has been contributing technical analysis, commentary and intelligence on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to Newswires since February 2006. Before this, Jerry spent 15 years as a senior interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market maker and bank proprietary trader; and 5 years as technical analyst in a brokerage firm.)\par \par \uc2 This is a financial news and information service. It is provided in general terms and does not take account of or address any individual user's position. To the extent that this article includes suggestions as to various possible investment strategies which users might consider, it does so in only general terms without reference to the personal factors which should determine any user's investment decisions. Nothing contained in this service constitutes personalized investment advice. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors shall not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article. This article does not constitute or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 29, 2014 01:29 ET (05:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 30-09-14 0137GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNWK00020140930ea9u00008\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
