\par\par \b \uc2 Data Confirms RBNZ Willing to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  in Market -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2014\par 05:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0320 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] The net sale of NZ$521 million by RBNZ in August confirms that the RBNZ is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times when the "\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is seen as unjustified and when market conditions are ripe for a successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says \uc2 Westpac\uc2  economist \uc2 Michael Gordon\uc2  . He adds that \uc2 Westpac\uc2  would not be surprised to see further selling over following months as market conditions are "clearly opportune given that sentiment has turned sharply against commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and in favor of the US dollar." He notes that the surprise statement released by the RBNZ last Thursday suggests that it still sees the NZD as unjustifiably high even after the fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to date. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0316 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] The \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  Index is off 1.95% as the market digests the impact of ongoing democracy protests in Hong Kong. \uc2 Francis Cheung\uc2  , head of China and Hong Kong strategy for CLSA, says the sell-off is irrational. "I don't think there will be an impact on the [local] economy and for mainland firms there is no impact. So the market correction makes no sense," says Cheung. He says Hongkong Land (H78.SG) would be the easiest stock on which to make a call, as it has the most real estate in Central that would be affected by prolonged civil disobedience. However, CLSA "really likes the stock" because it will benefit from the Hong Kong-Shanghai Stock Connect trading scheme, which will push up demand for Hong Kong office space. Cheung speculates that hedge funds may be jumping into the sell-off as it's just another reason to sell China equities given all the downbeat news lately about a decelerating economy. "For a hedge fudge fund there is little down-side risk. It's all negative news out there," says Cheung. (jasper.moiseiwitsch@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0316 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  has essentially "put its money where its mouth is" by shorting the New Zealand dollar at a time when the NZD was high and it expected it to fall, says ASB chief economist Nick Tuffley. "The RBNZ is being more active in its attempts to pull down the NZD through both talking more forcefully about the unsustainability of the high NZD and keeping the market off balance," he adds. RBNZ data shows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold a net NZ$521 million in August, the largest reduction in New Zealand dollar assets since July 2007. Tuffley adds ASB doesn't rule out further tactical actions from the RBNZ to keep downward pressure on the NZD; "Now that the NZD is trending down, it is easier to reinforce that trend than fight against an upward trend." (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0315 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The New Zealand dollar was hit hard in early Asia trading after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in August. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar dropped from around US$0.7865 to US$0.7770 on data from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  showing it had sold NZ$521 million in August. The Australian dollar was also caught in the kiwi's downdraft, pushing it closer to its one-year low of around US$0.8660. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: AAP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0302 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The Nikkei is up 0.4% at 16299.94 midday as the dollar consolidates most of its weekend gains (now at Y109.41). Investors are eyeing today's scheduled afternoon policy speech by Prime Minister Abe on his recently completed Cabinet re-jiggering for details on his goals. Beyond that, the July-Sep \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  tankan quarterly business survey result (due before the market open on Oct. 1) will have the greatest potential short-term sway on the market, says an equity trading director at a European brokerage. "Everybody remembers how bleak the Apr-Jun Tankan was; the question is if sentiment is getting worse for business or not, and how much the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can be counted on to accommodate a potentially worsening economic climate." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0302 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  released its official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statistics for August showing net selling of NZ$521 million, which likely constitutes material \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says Annette Beacher, head of Asia-Pacific Research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  . The amount of selling shows the "greater conviction" of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The New Zealand dollar was trading just above 0.7850, and fell to 0.7750 on the back of the announcement. Beacher says TD's year-end target remains at 0.8000. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0300 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Crude-oil futures are slightly lower in Asian trade Monday after ending mixed last week; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  WTI crude gained 2.06% last week and has been up for two consecutive weeks, while Brent crude lost 1.41% last week and has been down five of the past seven weeks. The recent strength in WTI has seen the Brent-WTI spread narrow to a fresh year low of less than $4 a barrel, ANZ says. "This may encourage traders outside the U.S. to take advantage of the spread and support gains in Brent," the bank says. WTI crude is down 61 cents at $92.93/bbl, Brent is down 30 cents at $96.70/bbl. (eric.yep@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0257 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The Chinese yuan falls as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the yuan fixing weaker to track the dollar's broad strength overseas. The yuan is at CNY6.1374 to a dollar from CNY6.1270 at Friday's close. The central parity is set at CNY6.1539 vs CNY6.1508 Friday. "In addition to the investors who are dollar bullish, many are buying the dollar to profit from the large spread from onshore and offshore swaps," says a Shanghai-based local bank trader. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY NDFs are up at 6.2520/6.2550 from 6.2415/6.2455 late Friday. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0239 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wharf Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0004.HK) leads declines on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index after police used tear gas against pro-democracy protesters on Sunday and economists point to a darkening outlook for department stores and other sellers of luxury goods. Wharf's shares fall 5.1% to HK$54.40, against a fall in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index of 2.2%. Today's retail sales statistics, due for release at 4.30pm Hong Kong Time, are expected to bring little respite. "Sales growth has been negative all year," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING\f28 \uc2 \f2  . The bank says Chinese President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2  's anti-corruption drive has contributed to the steepest decline in sales of jewellery, watches and valuable gifts since the SARS outbreak in 2003. This weekend's protests further darken the outlook: "We expect the battleground atmosphere on Hong Kong's streets to add to the drag on retail sales in September," \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING\f28 \uc2 \f2  adds. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter: @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0230 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] South Korea's current account surplus is on track to post a record high for this year even though it narrowed in August, says Jung Joon, director of the Bank of Korea's monetary and financial statistics division. The BOK in July forecast the country's annual current account surplus will reach $84 billion this year, the highest ever. "It is moving along the path as forecast," Jung notes after announcing the surplus in August narrowed to $7.27 billion from a revised $7.84 billion in July. The BOK says the softer August data were caused by strikes at local car manufacturers and seasonally growing overseas trips by Koreans. For the first eight months, the accumulated surplus is $54.31 billion. August marks the country's 30th straight month in surplus. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0217 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Tocom RSS3 rubber futures are lower with prices taking a hit after Shanghai opened to heavy losses. Qingdao rubber stocks have fallen to 155,000 tons as of last Friday--19% lower versus mid-September--but the destocking is not yet translating into real demand for the spot market as buyers are sitting on the sidelines in hopes of even lower prices, say traders. Benchmark March rubber trades Y3.6 lower at Y181.8/kg. (huileng.tan@wsj.com; Twitter: @huileng_tan) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0216 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Indonesia's rupiah tumbles to a 7-month low versus the U.S. dollar as USD/IDR rallies past its June peak of 12,105. The dual headwinds of a broadly stronger U.S. dollar and domestic political concerns are battering the rupiah. The U.S. dollar is consistently notching fresh 4-year highs versus the other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , thus exerting a bullish tone in the USD/Asia spectrum as well. Indonesian lawmakers' revoking of direct regional elections--seemingly a retaliatory move by opponents of president-elect Joko Widodo--takes the country a step away from democracy and is creating bearishness for the rupiah. The political challenge faced by Mr. Widodo may dim investors' hopes for economic and structural reforms. USD/IDR is now 12,125 versus its Friday close of 12,020. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 28, 2014 23:20 ET (03:20 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140929ea9t0007q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
