\par\par \b \uc2 NZ  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Done Yet, Says \uc2 UBS\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2014\par 06:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0422 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] Having confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not done yet, says Gareth Berry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  . The timing of the selling would seem "opportune" to launch an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign; with the U.S. dollar rallying across the board, the RBNZ is no longer fighting the current, and gets more bang for its buck," Berry said. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0420 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  expects to see Vietnam's economic fundamentals improve in 2015, thanks to low inflation and more activity in the country's domestic sector. So far this year foreign-invested exporters have been the driver behind Vietnam's growth, which accelerated 6.19% in the third quarter on year. The trade surplus year to date is $1.5 billion compared with a small deficit in the same period last year. But with inflation at five years lows, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is able to maintain low policy rates. \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  notes in a client research report that this in turn means "a lower debt-servicing burden for borrowers, which has supported further recovery in a deleveraging banking sector." That will likely encourage more lending going forward after a difficult few years, and stronger growth next year, \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  says. (james.hookway@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0416 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Hong Kong equities fall by the most in seven months as investors recoil from scenes of teargas being used on the city's streets. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index falls 1.9% to 23,218.64, on track for the worst intraday losses since February, while H-shares fare slightly better; the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2 China Enterprises\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index sinks 1.8% to 10,392.75. Data released during the weekend showed Chinese industrial profits fell 0.6% during August, the first decline in two years, while today's release of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  's China manufacturing PMI was delayed until Tuesday. CMC Markets says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  is now headed towards its 200-day simple moving average, a level which could trigger further selling. "A close below the 200 \f28 \uc2 \f2 SMA\f28 \uc2 \f2  at 23,158 will likely draw in further scrutiny ahead of the nation's holidays on 1st and 2nd October." (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter: @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0411 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] With only a handful of serviceable transport aircraft, the Philippine Air Force is seeking cost-effective ways to boost its airlift capacity. A meeting between President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Benigno Aquino\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus\f28 \uc2 \f2  (EADSY) executives during Aquino's visit to France last week has fuelled speculation that the Philippines is emerging as a likely customer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus Military\f28 \uc2 \f2  's A400M transport plane. This would build on a relationship that saw Manila order three smaller transports, worth $118 million, from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus Military\f28 \uc2 \f2  earlier this year. But at $190 million per plane, the A400M is beyond Manila's means, at least for now, and cheaper options are being pursued in the medium term. One such option is used aircraft sourced from friendly countries, and a \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  official in Manila has confirmed that Washington is currently expediting the sale of two second-hand C-130 Hercules transports to the Philippines--with other surplus kit likely to follow later, the official said. (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0406 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Vietnam's economic growth is expected to accelerate further in the fourth quarter, Deputy Minister of Planning and Investment Cao Viet Sinh says. "Imports of equipment and materials for domestic production are on the rise...and firms are receiving more orders, suggesting production is recovering," Sinh says. He says Vietnam will meet its growth target of 5.8% for this year, after government data released Friday shows the economy grew 5.62% on year in the Jan-Sep period. Growth in the third quarter quickened to 6.19% from 5.42% in the second quarter. However, Sinh says he's concerned about high levels of bad debt at banks and a sluggish pace of banks' lending. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0403 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] One year on, the Shanghai free trade zone has failed to impress many business executives hoping for bolder reforms. "I still don't find the FTZ as a physical entity very exciting because one year on, I would expect more to have happened," said Fredrik H\u228\'00\'E4hnel, general manager of merchant banking at the Shanghai branch of Nordic lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  . Mr. H\u228\'00\'E4hnel said he had hoped for breakthroughs such as the permission for companies to issue yuan-denominated bonds in the free-trade zone and full access for wholly owned foreign investment banks or brokerage firms to China's domestic capital markets. He added that SEB isn't considering setting up a branch in the free-zone now. "We don't see anything we can do in the FTZ that we can't do outside now.... But if we see fundamental changes, such as total access to offshore funding or the capital markets, we'll look into it," he said. (hong.shen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0356 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The recent removal of the project's leader, Dai Haibo, marked the latest setback for the much-hyped Shanghai free-trade zone. Dai's sacking two weeks ago came just as China geared up for the one-year anniversary of the pilot project. The government gave no reason for Dai's removal but state-run media have reported that he is under investigation for alleged corruption. On Friday, Shanghai's vice mayor, Ai Baojun, said at a news conference that Dai's removal was a "normal personnel shift". Within hours of Dai's removal, the the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Gold Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced that it would move up the launch date of an international trading platform in the free trade zone to September 18 instead of on today's anniversary. (hong.shen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0331 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The Shanghai free-trade zone, promoted as a landmark effort to remake China's economy, has little to celebrate on its one-year anniversary. Reforms so far have mainly focused on cutting red tape for businesses and opening up certain industries to investment, but eagerly anticipated liberalization of interest rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mechanisms have fallen well short of expectations. "Progress on the Shanghai FTZ has been quite modest, even by the low standards of China's gradual and incremental approach to market-oriented and financial-sector reforms," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eswar Prasad\f28 \uc2 \f2  , a China expert at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cornell University\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (hong.shen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JVW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0323 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  says don't worry too much about the Hong Kong pro-democracy protests from a creditworthiness point of view. The agency says it won't change the territory's AA+ rating with stable outlook unless the protests deepen. "It would be negative if the protests are on a wide enough scale and last long enough to have a material effect on the economy or financial stability, but we don't currently see this as very likely," said Andrew Colquhoun, head of sovereign ratings at Fitch in Asia. The firm cited the government's strong balance sheet and high standards of governance as positives. There's likely some short-term impact on retailers, who already were suffering from China's anti-graft crackdown. But how this will play out in the longer run for now is unclear. (tom.wright@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0321 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The Indonesian parliamentary budget committee's approval last week to reduce energy subsidies to 344.7 trillion rupiah ($28.4 billion) in 2015 from 350.3 trillion rupiah allocated for this year is credit-positive for Indonesia, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "Although the steps are modest in economic terms, they signal a political shift toward greater fiscal discipline," it says, noting that this would reverse five straight years of rising subsidies. The budget plan would narrow the 2015 budget deficit to 2.2%. (I-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JVW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0320 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The net sale of NZ$521 million by RBNZ in August confirms that the RBNZ is willing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at times when the "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar is seen as unjustified and when market conditions are ripe for a successful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michael Gordon\f28 \uc2 \f2  . He adds that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  would not be surprised to see further selling over following months as market conditions are "clearly opportune given that sentiment has turned sharply against commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and in favor of the US dollar." He notes that the surprise statement released by the RBNZ last Thursday suggests that it still sees the NZD as unjustifiably high even after the fall in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to date. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0316 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index is off 1.95% as the market digests the impact of ongoing democracy protests in Hong Kong. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Francis Cheung\f28 \uc2 \f2  , head of China and Hong Kong strategy for CLSA, says the sell-off is irrational. "I don't think there will be an impact on the [local] economy and for mainland firms there is no impact. So the market correction makes no sense," says Cheung. He says Hongkong Land (H78.SG) would be the easiest stock on which to make a call, as it has the most real estate in Central that would be affected by prolonged civil disobedience. However, CLSA "really likes the stock" because it will benefit from the Hong Kong-Shanghai Stock Connect trading scheme, which will push up demand for Hong Kong office space. Cheung speculates that hedge funds may be jumping into the sell-off as it's just another reason to sell China equities given all the downbeat news lately about a decelerating economy. "For a hedge fudge fund there is little down-side risk. It's all negative news out there," says Cheung. (jasper.moiseiwitsch@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 29, 2014 00:22 ET (04:22 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140929ea9t000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
