\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Falls to Lowest Level in Over a Year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer and James Ramage   \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2014\par 01:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Korean (English)\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar touched its lowest level against the U.S. dollar in more than a year on Monday after data showed the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold large amounts of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, increasing expectations of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net 521 million New Zealand dollars (US$409.8 million) in August, the most since July 2007, and significantly more than the NZ$2 million it sold in July this year, data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply after the data's release, touching US$0.7708, its weakest since early August 2013, according to CQG, from around US$0.7828 just before the release. In late New York trade, the kiwi, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also called, fell 1.2% versus the dollar, to US$0.7770, and 1.1% against the yen, to Yen85.03.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "put its money where its mouth is" by selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ASB chief economist Nick Tuffley said. "We don't rule out further tactical actions from the RBNZ to keep downward pressure on the New Zealand dollar."\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has said on several occasions that the New Zealand dollar was unjustifiably strong even given the country's relatively robust economy. Market participants have interpreted the statements as indications that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to weaken the kiwi.\par \par \uc2 "We think kiwi remains 15% to 20% overvalued; there's significant scope for further adjustments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if economic fundamentals in New Zealand deteriorate from here," said Aroop Chatterjee, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  quantitative strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 . "Also, weakening demand from a key export market like China would add to worries about the New Zealand dollar, and push back any potential rate hikes from the RBNZ."\par \par \uc2 The kiwi's gains are largely the result of an economy that has outperformed those of most other developed nations since the global financial crisis. The South Pacific nation, with a population of 4.5 million, has benefited from booming Asian demand for its meat and dairy exports, and the pace of its economic growth is now at a 10-year high.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand is also among the few countries to have begun a cycle of interest-rate increases--four so far this year--helping fuel demand for the kiwi.\par \par \uc2 Still, cracks are starting to show in the economy. Among the biggest concerns is a sharp decline in prices of milk and dairy products, the country's largest export sector.\par \par \uc2 Theo Spierings\uc2 , chief executive at dairy giant \uc2 Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd\uc2 ., said any decline in the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help exporters.\par \par \uc2 Also in Monday's trade, the dollar climbed 0.1% versus the yen, to Yen109.44. During Asian trade, the dollar hit a fresh six-year high against the yen, reaching Yen109.75. The euro held steady versus the greenback, at $1.2692.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at Lucy.Craymer@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 29, 2014 16:16 ET (20:16 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 29-09-14 2322GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNWK00020140929ea9t0001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
