\par\par \b \uc2 Challenges of Governing in a Weak Global Economy -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2014\par 13:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:25 EDT - The challenges of governing in a weak global economy were on display Monday. Most strikingly, the protests that have gripped Hong Kong speak to the difficulty that China has in trying to sustain the \uc2 Communist Party\uc2 's centralized control over power and the economy while also seeking to take a leadership role in the global economy. But it's also evident in much smaller \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its earlier rate hikes attracted funds into its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , funds that had been created by bigger central banks. And in Europe, the forces of deflation stirred by regional and global economic stagnation showed their influence in consumer price data from Germany and Spain. (michael.casey@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 6:54 EDT - Cal-Maine's (CALM) fiscal 1Q sales climb 12% from the prior year driven by higher egg volume and prices. Company says specialty egg sales account for 18.8% of the number of eggs sold and 26.8% of its egg revenue. While CALM is receiving higher prices for its eggs, feed costs fell 11% from the year earlier, though it says prices remain high historically for soybean meal. CALM expects demand to remain strong but warns high supply could pressure prices this year. Shares, inactive premarket, are up 42% YTD. (patrick.sullivan@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com \par Cynthia Lin, 212 416-4403, Cynthia.lin@wsj.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181, john.shipman@wsj.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326, Patrick.sullivan@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 29, 2014 07:26 ET (11:26 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140929ea9t00187\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
