\par\par \b \uc2 Australian Dollar Caught in Wheels of NZ$  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Glynn   \par \uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2014\par 07:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY--The Australian dollar continued to be crunched Monday, falling to an 8-month low after being caught in a downdraft generated by a plunging \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, moving to protect the country's exporters from sharply falling commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar has tended lately to be caught up in moves by the New Zealand dollar due to its regional proximity and the fact that it too is a commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite a sharp fall through September, \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still likely hoping for further falls in the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold a net 521 million New Zealand dollars (US$404.5 million) in August. This was the largest reduction in New Zealand dollar assets since July 2007 and significantly higher than the NZ$2 million it sold in July.\par \par \uc2 At 0500 GMT, the Australian dollar changed hands at US$0.8699, compared with US$0.8755 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Been, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2  said the "negative Aussie dollar" story remains intact as the price of iron ore continues to weaken. The price of iron ore has fallen by more than 40% in 2014.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar is now within reach of its 2014 low of US$0.8660.\par \par \uc2 Traders are now awaiting data Tuesday on Chinese manufacturing and U.S. payrolls at the end of the week. Any hints of further slowdown in China, or improvement in U.S. employment, might see the Aussie dollar test fresh lows, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Local data this week includes retail sales and building approvals data for August. The reports will provide an update on the pace of economic recovery in the non-mining parts of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of a hike in interest rates by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  any time soon are low, so the domestic reports will likely have little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -Write to James Glynn at james.glynn@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 29-09-14 0553GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140929ea9t0005e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
