\par\par \b \uc2 Australia, NZ dlrs mauled by return of volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2014\par 04:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * NZ dlr near one-year trough in wake of RBNZ warning\par \par \uc2 * Aussie slugged by spike in volatility, risk aversion\par \par \uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu and Wayne Cole\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars were nursing heavy losses on Friday after a spasm of risk aversion bludgeoned commodity prices and spooked investors out of carry trades.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie was nailed down at $0.8805, having struck an eight-month low of $0.8774 overnight.\par \par \uc2 That left losses for the month at 5.6 percent, the biggest since May last year and another period when global markets were roiled by speculation about higher U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed a slight bounce to $0.7950 on Friday after hitting a one-year low of $0.7912.\par \par \uc2 It sank almost 2 percent on Thursday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which it said was still 'unjustifiably" high.\par \par \uc2 "The RBNZ has certainly been a lot more vocal, and we would expect them to put their money where the mouth is, now that things are going their way," ANZ analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release figures on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in August, when a big drop in the kiwi during illiquid trading triggered rumours it may have entered the market to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also been undermined by a spike in market volatility which makes life hard for carry traders, who borrow at low rates in yen and euros to buy the higher yielding Aussie and kiwi.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie shed 1.3 percent on the yen on Thursday, while the kiwi dived 2.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said there was no single catalyst for the moves, but rather a laundry list of possible triggers including reports Russia might freeze foreign assets in retaliation for sanctions, worries about growth in China, conflict in the Middle East and profit taking for the quarter end.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was particularly hard hit, slumping to 77.04 against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the weakest since early February.\par \par \uc2 Traders said demand from exporters was supporting the kiwi for now, but added that the break below $0.8000 had opened the door to a test of $0.7670, a trough hit in August last year.\par \par \uc2 "Levels around $0.7900-$0.7925 have some value on the day, but the market's going to be concentrating on levels to sell," said Tim Kelleher, head of institutional sales at ASB, adding that any upside would be limited by offers looming in the $0.7950-$0.7980 region.\par \par \uc2 "If we see a drift back up towards those levels today, I expect to see some selling."\par \par \uc2 Technical signs suggested that a decisive break of $0.7930, which contains trendline support drawn from its 2011 and 2013 troughs, will offer a further signal to sell.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi has dropped more than 10 percent since July on expectations that the RBNZ will wait until early next year to resume raising interest rates, while brewing speculation that U.S. rates may start rising next year has boosted the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The return of risk aversion globally gave a fillip to government bond markets. Yields on New Zealand debt was as much as 3 basis point slower for longer dated paper.\par \par \uc2 Three-year Australian bond futures added 3 ticks to 97.200, while the 10-year contract gained 6 ticks to 96.450. (Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-26T03:35:14.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140926ea9q001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
