\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Tumbles on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Comments -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2014\par 06:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--The New Zealand dollar fell to its lowest levels in over a year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated the exchange rate is "unjustified and unsustainable" and added that these are important considerations when assessing whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is feasible.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said the exchange rate is susceptible to a "significant downward adjustment" and the bank would welcome a move toward a sustainable level.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell sharply on the comments and touched US$0.7995, its weakest since early September 2013, from around US$0.8070 just prior to the comments.\par \par \uc2 The Kiwi is off the near record highs it reached in July but "the New Zealand dollar exchange rate is at exceptional levels compared with its history," said Mr. Wheeler Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar's strength is largely a result of the country's strong performance relative to other developed nations since the global financial crisis. The South Pacific nation, with a population of just 4.5 million, has benefited from booming Asian demand for its meat and dairy exports.\par \par \uc2 The economy has outpaced the U.K. and U.S. in recent times and growth is currently at a 10-year high. New Zealand is among the few countries to have begun a cycle of rate increases--four so far this year--while other comparable countries still have theirs near zero, helping fuel demand for the Kiwi.\par \par \uc2 However, "even allowing for New Zealand's economic outperformance relative to most advanced economies, New Zealand's real effective exchange rate is above the level that can be justified," Mr. Wheeler said Friday. The REER takes into account inflation and the relative strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's main trade partners.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the exchange rate becomes exceptionally high or low, or if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level is seen as "unjustified"--meaning it is at odds with prevailing economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 Regarding possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, he also noted that "another consideration is whether conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are conducive to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  having an impact on the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Wheeler has made several similar comments over the past few months, leading to speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "clearly stepping up their focus toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and believe it is creating imbalances in the economy at the current level," said Sam Tuck, an Auckland-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ANZ.\par \par \uc2 Stuart Ive, Wellington-based client adviser for \uc2 OM Financial\uc2 , said the New Zealand dollar was likely to remain under pressure into the European session. However, he didn't think immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the cards because of Governor Wheeler's comments.\par \par \uc2 "You wouldn't talk it lower before you sell it," said Mr. Ive.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 25, 2014 00:47 ET (04:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140925ea9p000ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
