\par\par \b \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  of N.Z. Remarks Keep  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  on Table -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2014\par 05:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to classify the current level of the NZD as "unjustified and unsustainable" which ensures "the potential of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on the table," says ANZ Senior Manager \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sam Tuck. He notes Governor Wheeler "preferred not to comment" when questioned if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Investors will be keeping an eye out for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data--RBNZ foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets and liabilities--due at the end of the month to find out if they have been in the market, says Tuck. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @FarroHoward) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0345 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Thailand's stock exchange becomes the first exchange in Southeast Asia to partner with the \uc2 UN\uc2  Sustainable Stock Exchanges Initiative. The program is aimed at enhancing corporate transparency and performance in environmental and social issues, as well as governance in order to promote the sustainability in trade on stock markets around the world. The Stock Exchange of Thailand is also hoping to draw in more foreign investors by joining the initiative. "We want to tell the world that all products available at any exchanges participating in this initiative (including the Thai market) will be there for long-term sustainable trade," says Bordin Unakul, a vice president at the SET. To date, 13 stock exchanges worldwide, including \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  and \uc2 NYSE\uc2  in the U.S., have made commitment with the \uc2 UN\uc2  SSE Initiative.(nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0343 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] While New Zealand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to maintain a tightening bias, suggesting that "some further policy tightening will be necessary", it has clearly adopted a "more mild tone", says First NZ Capital \f28 \uc2 \f2 Economist\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chris Green. It "reinforces our expectation that the OCR [Official Cash Rate] is likely to remain unchanged until the first half of 2015," he says. Green is tipping a 25 basis point increase in the OCR to 3.75% following the release of the June 2015 monetary policy statement. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @FarroHoward) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0336 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's cellphone operators will benefit from a decision by India's federal cabinet of ministers to fund the expansion of cellular telephone networks in the country's northeastern region. India's federal cabinet decided late Wednesday that it would spend 53.36 billion rupees ($877.5 million) to set up networks in the region. The number of cellphone users in the region is far below the national average of about 74%. The expansion of telecom networks will also include national highways in the same area, according to the cabinet decision. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532454.BY), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Idea Cellular\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532822.BY), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Communications (532712.BY) \f28 \uc2 \f2 and the Indian units of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (VOD.LN) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telenor (TEL.OS) \f28 \uc2 \f2 provide cellphone services in the northeast. (krishna.jai@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @jaikrishna) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] With USD/JPY rising to as high as 106.89, a fresh 6-year high, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair should surpass 110 as the U.S. economy expands and the U.S. Federal Reserve Bank heads towards interest rate hikes, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Even if the Nikkei reaches 17500, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  will not likely halt quantitative easing until it achieves its 2% inflation target," says house strategist Taisuke Tanaka. "While tailwinds for risk-on investing gather strength and the BOJ makes an unprecedented leap, USD/JPY could hold at 100 or 110 if these conditions persist for multiple years." However, it would not be surprising if USD/JPY overshoots to the 120 level in 2015-16, he adds.(bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0325 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The lowest accepted price for 5-year JGBs at the 0345 GMT auction result is likely around 100.09, traders say. The latest No. 120 issue carries a 0.2% coupon, unchanged from the previous issue. SMBC Nikko Securities strategist Soichi Takeyama expects a firm auction, aided by low \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  discount bill yields that have supported demand in the mid- and short-term sectors. The fact the BOJ hasn't been attracting the latest 5-year issue in its buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also "a sign of investor demand and firm demand to hold onto the current issue." Lead December JGB futures are down 0.16 at 145.49 at the midday close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (eleanor.warnock@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0323 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The market is taking USD/JPY higher alongside rising U.S. bond yields ahead of next week's FOMC meeting amid speculation that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may change the language in the FOMC statement to a more hawkish tone, DBS says. But the bank notes that U.S. interest rate futures have remained more stable than bonds, suggesting that it may be premature for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  to shift its forward guidance before it completes tapering asset purchases in October. DBS says that the latest U.S. monthly payrolls report after all did disappoint and data Wednesday showed U.S. mortgage applications fell to a 14-year low last week with the U.S. Mortgage Bankers Association's market composite index at its lowest level since December 2000. Hence, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  may wait till the FOMC meeting in December before it shifts to a less dovish stance, DBS says. (jerry.tan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Leong\f28 \uc2 \f2  IB says Malaysia stocks are likely to stay in tight range ahead of next week's closely-watched monetary policy meetings; U.S. Federal Open Market Committee is scheduled to meet September 16 while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will announce its monetary policy review September 18. "Overall, any unfavourable hawkish tone on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's future interest rate hike timeframe and should BNM decided to introduce another hike in its overnight policy rate could usher in wild swings into the markets," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Leong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , tipping near-term technical resistance at 1876-1886 and support at 1850-1860. Malaysia KLCI is currently up 0.1% at 1873.16. (jason.ng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0312 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Nikkei is up 0.5% at 15864.44 midday as the dollar comes off its highs (now at Y106.73). Major investors have set up positions that will stay profitable as long as the Nikkei remains below the 16000 strike price for September index options and futures, which expire tomorrow, says an equity trading director at a European brokerage. "Investment banks will sell the cash market as much as possible to keep the those positions viable for the time being, so there likely isn't much more upside for the market through tomorrow," he says. He adds that Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's meeting around noon with Bank of Japan Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  to discuss the country's economic conditions will be closely monitored for comments that may affect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0310 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Crude oil futures were trading sideways in Asian trade. After edging below $100 per barrel, Brent crude continued to trade below that level. There are expectations that that Saudi Arabia could cut oil production in response to weak prices. Brent crude was at $98.24/bbl, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  was at $91.85/bbl.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0303 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vietnam Joint Stock Commercial Bank for Industry and Trade\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CTG.VH), or \f28 \uc2 \f2 VietinBank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , signed an agreement for a $50 million syndicated loan from four foreign banks led by Cathay United Bank as it is building up funds in anticipation of a faster economic recovery, \f28 \uc2 \f2 VietinBank\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO Le Duc Tho says. "The economic recovery is expected to accelerate and demand for loans will increase," Tho says, adding that the loan deal, signed Wednesday, shows that foreign investors have confidence in his bank. He adds that \f28 \uc2 \f2 VietinBank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also keeping an eye on the possibility of selling dollar-denominated bonds in the international market. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0303 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's yuan fell Thursday morning after hitting six-month highs in two sessions in a row, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the fixing at a slightly weaker level. The yuan is at 6.1316 to a dollar, compared with 6.1299 at Wednesday's close. The central parity is set at 6.1453 versus 6.1425 Wednesday. "After guiding the yuan stronger for two days, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is taking a break. As it always said, it wants two-way volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY non-deliverable forwards are up at 6.2230/6.2260 from 6.2160/6.2210 late Wednesday. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 10, 2014 23:54 ET (03:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140911ea9b000gb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
