\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Down Late on Worries of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2014\par 07:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is down late Monday after falling late last week when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fueled speculation it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar now nearly US$0.2 lower than it was before that comment Thursday, market players now think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar "continues to be well behaved" the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2  senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Sam Tuck said.\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8535 compared with US$0.8577 late Friday. The New Zealand dollar was at 0.9092 Australian dollars compared with 0.9113 Australian dollars late Friday.\par \par \uc2 This week will be driven by the U.S. dollar with advance second-quarter U.S. GDP data, a statement from the Federal Reserve, nonfarm payrolls data and the ISM manufacturing data all scheduled, Mr. Tuck said.\par \par \uc2 Locally Fonterra Dairy Co-operative is expected to upgrade its milk payout forecast. It forecast in late May that it will pay 7.00 New Zealand dollars a kilo of milk solids but as international dairy prices have continued to fall and the New Zealand dollar has remained resilient banks have downgraded what they expect the company to be able to pay.\par \par \uc2 "A decline to 6.20 New Zealand dollars would eventually take roughly 4 billion New Zealand dollars revenue out of the dairy sector although farmer cashflow will remain firm for a good while yet given the structure of payments," \uc2 Bank of New Zealand\uc2  said. It added a lowering of milk price expectations will highlight strength in the New Zealand dollar is unjustified.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com, @lucy_craymer\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 28, 2014 01:21 ET (05:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140728ea7s0009g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
