\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Consolidating After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Jitters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2014\par 07:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar spent Friday in a tight range after taking a tumble Thursday when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelled speculation that it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 "It was always going to be about consolidation today as the market takes on board comments from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including overtones that they are willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the situation warrants it," said OM Financial client advisor, Stuart Ive.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Reserve Bank Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  described the Kiwi dollar's strength as "unjustified and unsustainable," and the use of the word "unjustifiable" was widely viewed as a strong indication that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can opt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the exchange rate becomes exceptionally high or low, or if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level is seen as "unjustified"-which means at odds with prevailing economic conditions. The comment was "a bold and direct warning about the level of the NZD," said BNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Kymberly Martin.\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8577 compared with US$0.8587 late Thursday and US$0.8581 early Friday. The New Zealand dollar was at A$0.9113 against the Australian dollar versus A$0.9085 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 It largely overlooked news that New Zealand business confidence continued to wane in July according \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 's business outlook survey, given how far it fell after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments, said Mr. Ive.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead next week is marked by an "exceptional amount of U.S. data" that will drive the Kiwi, including the gross domestic product, that Federal Open Market Committee statement, and employment data, said Mr. Ive. Domestically the GlobalDairyTrade auction will be closely watched and any further weakness in dairy prices will also weigh on the Kiwi, he added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 25, 2014 01:07 ET (05:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140725ea7p000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
