\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Down Late as RBNZ Comments Cause Selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2014\par 08:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar was trading sharply lower late Thursday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  increased the cash rate 25 basis points but signalled it would hold rates now to assess the impact of increases.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Gov. Graeme Wheeler said in a statement the economy appeared to be adjusting to the monetary policy tightening and "it is prudent that there now be a period of assessment before rates adjust further towards a more-neutral level."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started its tightening cycle in March and has since raised the official cash rate one percentage point to 3.50%.\par \par \uc2 Western Union\uc2  Business Solutions corporate dealing manager Chris Hunter said the increasing likelihood that interest rates may be on hold for some time had caused some selling in the New Zealand dollar.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ, in its monetary policy statement, described the Kiwi dollar's strength as "unjustified and unsustainable," which was widely seen as firing the first shot in a new war aimed at lowering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the stubborn strength of which continues to hobble the nation's exporters.\par \par \uc2 "We interpret this as a direct warning that the RBNZ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars," said \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 .'s New Zealand chief economist, Dominick Stephens.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar did tick slightly higher following the release of strong China manufacturing data, but this was short-lived as investors returned to selling on the RBNZ comments.\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8587 compared with US$0.8681 late Wednesday. The New Zealand dollar was at A$0.9085 against the Australian dollar versus A$0.9202.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com, @lucy_craymer\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 24, 2014 02:21 ET (06:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140724ea7o000l0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
