\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Raises Eyebrows With Dollar Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 By \u8201\'20\'09Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2014\par 07:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand-The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to raise interest rates Thursday was largely anticipated by the markets. Its stance on the soaring local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though, took them by surprise.\par \par \uc2 Describing the Kiwi dollar's strength as "unjustified and unsustainable," the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  was widely seen as firing the first shot in a new war aimed at lowering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the stubborn strength of which continues to hobble the nation's exporters.\par \par \uc2 "We interpret this as a direct warning that the RBNZ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars," said \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 .'s New Zealand chief economist, Dominick Stephens. The New Zealand dollar shed close to one U.S. cent after the statement to trade as low as $0.8591.\par \par \uc2 The Kiwi has come off the 30-year peak it touched in early July, but is still trading at historically high levels. It is about 1.8% higher against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  than in April 2013, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the time, the Kiwi moved slightly lower but the impact was short-lived.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar's strength has everything to do with the country's strong performance relative to other developed nations since the global financial crisis. The South Pacific island, with a population of just 4.5 million, has benefited from booming Asian demand for its meat and dairy exports.\par \par \uc2 The economy has outpaced the U.K. and U.S. in recent times, growing by 3.3% in the year through March. New Zealand is among the few countries to have begun a cycle of rate increases-four so far this year-while other comparable countries still have theirs near zero.\par \par \uc2 It is little surprise, then, that New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has looked relatively attractive for some time. Money has flowed into the country more recently as recoveries in other developed economies have looked less convincing.\par \par \uc2 Now, though, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is worried the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -among the world's 10-most traded-may sour the economic gains made so far, at a time when prices for commodities like dairy and timber, another key New Zealand export, have been dropping.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the exchange rate becomes exceptionally high or low, or if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level is seen as "unjustified"-which means at odds with prevailing economic conditions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also only allowable if it has a reasonable chance of success in moving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the desired level, and as long as it doesn't prevent the bank achieving its own inflation target.\par \par \uc2 Darren Gibbs, chief economist at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in New Zealand, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's language on Thursday suggested it was more open than before to selling some of its Kiwi holdings\par \par \uc2 Still, the reserve bank's ability to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited because of the amount of New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it holds. The nation's finance minister, Bill English, has compared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to "a peashooter in a war zone."\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 24, 2014 01:52 ET (05:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140724ea7o000h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
