\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Kiwi rattled by  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  warning, dollar steadies\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 14:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds more comment)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar falls from highs after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warning\par \par \uc2 * Dollar steadies but still broadly weak\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine crisis supports safe-haven bid for yen\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on Yellen speech for more clues on Fed's rate path\par \par \uc2 By Patrick Graham\par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 7 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar was the main mover on developed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday, falling almost one percent after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted by rises in official interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  has led its peers this year in raising interest rates, driving a 13 percent rally for the kiwi against the U.S. dollar since last August.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure so far to make good on predictions of a surge this year - it languished close to six-month lows against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday - have helped extend that rise.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 , who \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at slightly weaker levels a year ago, said the bank could sell the kiwi if it stayed strong in the face of worse fundamentals such as a further fall in export prices.\par \par \uc2 He also said further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength would be a factor in future moves on interest rates although several strategists in London cast doubt on whether that would prevent the bank from hiking official rates further.\par \par \uc2 "The question for the last three months has been whether there was too much good news in the price for the kiwi ... clearly some of that has come into play," said \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2 , strategist with \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "New Zealand's fundamentals are still strong enough to justify (buying the kiwi) but perhaps there is less reason to be gung ho on interest rates than before and pushing toward 88 per dollar is going to be a little bit more difficult from here."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadied somewhat ahead of U.S. markets opening but was still down 0.7 percent on the day to trade at $0.8675, more than a cent below almost three-year high of $0.8779 hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Still, the message from most analysts remained fairly positive.\par \par \uc2 "I would be reluctant to go too far with the story markets have bought into overnight," said \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy with \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "On \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it is a warning but I don't read it as a threat or a clear signal they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 FED TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar took a step lower when London returned from a holiday on Tuesday and investors are braced for the possibility that dovish comments from Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  could further undermine the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new chief is widely expected to hammer home its dovish position at her congressional hearings on Wednesday and Thursday, even after last Friday's upbeat U.S. payrolls report.\par \par \uc2 "Yellen does have the potential to inject some life into the dollar but I think she is going to be cagey," said Foley.\par \par \uc2 "The market needs to be convinced that the Fed is going to raise rates earlier than it currently does. We need some more and better data (to do that). For now everyone looks happy to sell any dollar rallies."\par \par \uc2 Many analysts and traders view the Fed's communication since Yellen's arrival as somewhat garbled. An initial nod towards a rise in interest rates in the first half of next year was quickly talked down by policymakers and there is little faith the Fed will follow its reining-in of bond-buying with actual rate rises anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 That, along with flows of capital into European capital markets and the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inability to take more concrete action to weaken the euro, has left this year's predictions for a stronger dollar looking exposed.\par \par \uc2 "It now seems quite likely that we could see a test of $1.40 (per euro) very soon, especially if we break the strong resistance level at 1.3967 - the 2014 high," \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  analysts said in a morning note. "The Yellen speech or inaction from the ECB (at a policy meeting) tomorrow could be potential triggers."\par \par \uc2 Against the euro the dollar was steady at $1.3927, within sight of two-month highs of $1.3952 hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered from a three-week low of 101.43 yen to trade flat on the day at 101.69. The dollar index was last at 79.135, up slightly on the day but not far from the previous session's trough of 79.060. (Editing by Pravin Char)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-10T12:00:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140507ea5700m84\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
