\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2 -NZ cenbank gov warns of  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2 , rate hikes might slow\b0\par\par\uc2 974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBNZ Gov says NZ$ over-valued and unsustainable\par \par \uc2 * RBNZ could sell NZ$ if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not weaken\par \par \uc2 * High \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  factor may slow future rate rises   (Recasts, adds details, quotes, updates market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Gyles Beckford\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, May 7 (Reuters) - New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday warned that it may have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the country's high-flying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and suggested interest rate hikes might be slowed if the kiwi dollar remains elevated.\par \par \uc2 The forthright comments by Reserve Bank of New Zealand  governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  sent the New Zealand dollar -- the 10th most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally -- skidding nearly half a U.S. cent, as markets adjusted to the prospect of a less aggressive tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains high in the face of worsening fundamentals, such as a continued weakening in export prices, it would become more opportune for the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars," Wheeler said in a speech to a dairy farming conference.\par \par \uc2 Wheeler said a stubbornly strong New Zealand dollar "will be a factor in our assessment of the extent and speed with which the Official Cash Rate needs to be raised."\par \par \uc2 Analysts were quick to note that the RBNZ has made similar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings in the past, but the implications for interest rates weren't lost on domestic markets.\par \par \uc2 "We do expect that sustained NZ dollar strength will slow the tightening cycle this year," said ASB Bank chief economist Nick Tuffley, who is picking another 25 basis point hike in June.  "But, beyond June, continued NZ dollar strength would reinforce our view that the RBNZ would pause until the end of the year."\par \par \uc2 Faced with rising inflation pressures in a booming economy, the RBNZ started its long-awaited rate-tightening cycle in March, becoming the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a developed economy to raise rates. Wheeler's latest comments suggest the bank may not apply the brakes too hard.\par \par \uc2 Another 25-basis-point hike at the June meeting would lift the cash rate to 3.25 percent, following similar-sized hikes in March and April, but a prolonged pause beyond that point would leave rates much lower than the RBNZ's implied projection of 4.25 percent by year-end.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower its projection on interest rates in June.\par \par \uc2 "Were the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold at current levels, moving into the June MPS forecast round, there would be scope for inflation forecast downgrades, which should also cascade into the RBNZ's rate track," \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  senior economist Ben Jarman said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL KIWI\par \par \uc2 The kiwi, one of the 10 most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally, has been boosted by dairy export driven terms of trade at 40 year highs, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resumption of rate rises boosting its yield attraction for investors in carry trades.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  carry traders borrow in countries with low interest costs to fund purchases in markets with higher yields. At 3.00 percent New Zealand's rates are well above the Fed fund's rate of 0.0 to 0.25 percent and even that of Australia which is at 2.50 percent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  arsenal is dwarfed by the massive global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, with more than 100 billion New Zealand dollars traded daily -- meaning interest rates remain the biggest tool to manage the kiwi.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has talked \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past and occasionally sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in modest amounts, but Wheeler's comments were his most assertive piece of jawboning since he became governor in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "We are closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It would not be a surprise if they were to do it one day," said \uc2 Westpac\uc2  senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Imre Speizer.\par \par \uc2 "It's stronger rhetoric against the exchange rate than we have seen from this governor yet."\par \par \uc2 Wheeler said the kiwi, which hit a two-and-a half year high of $0.8779 on Tuesday, was overvalued and unsustainable at current levels\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be expected to weaken if the Chinese economy were to slow, global dairy prices fall, financial market volatility was to return, and the U.S. economy improved.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi dropped to a low of $0.8700 from $0.8740. It last traded at $0.8690. So far this year it has risen about 5.8 percent against the U.S. dollar, and in March a visiting IMF team said it was overvalued by as much as 15 percent.\par \par \uc2 RBNZ POWERLESS\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has regularly voiced its concern about the high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but has also admitted that it's largely powerless to affect the value other than at the margins, and that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be to remind investors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not a one way bet".\par \par \uc2 A year ago, Wheeler made a similar sort of speech and disclosed the RBNZ had sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in five years.\par \par \uc2 Dairy products provided about a third of the country's NZ$50 billion export earnings in the year to March, with China the biggest buyer. But prices have fallen more than 20 percent over the past two months, and the high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a headwind to export earnings.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 17 economists shows all but one expect the RBNZ to raise rates to 3.25 percent in June, and though most economists anticipate rates to rise to 3.75 percent by the end of the year, Wheeler's comment puts the more aggressive market forecasts in perspective.\par \par \uc2 The "dairy price dynamics are now bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into sharper focus," \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's Jarman said, and that would feed into a more modest interest rate tightening track.        (Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-10T03:35:49.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140506ea5600zne\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
