\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Falls After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Talk of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 10:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell Wednesday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it, but the bank's plan to continue raising interest rates will make engineering a decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a challenge over the long term.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Graeme Wheeler said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to take action to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , among the world's best-performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, to prevent its strength from choking off exports ranging from fruit to wine.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains high in the face of worsening fundamentals, such as a continued weakening in export prices, it would become more opportune for the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars," he told a conference of dairy farmers.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, known as the kiwi, dropped nearly half a cent against the U.S. dollar following his comments, to US$0.8702.\par \par \uc2 Keith Poore, head of investment strategy for AMP Capital New Zealand, which has more than 18.0 billion New Zealand dollars (US$15.6 billion) under management in the country, said Mr. Wheeler's comments added to rising risks facing the kiwi in the near term. Those risks include falling prices of milk, New Zealand's biggest export.\par \par \uc2 "At the current level there is definitely reason for the kiwi to move lower," said Mr. Poore, who has been a seller of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the past month.\par \par \uc2 Still, the kiwi remains up nearly 4% this year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that includes the U.S. dollar and British pound, partly due to record-high terms of trade as the New Zealand's agriculture-rich economy feeds Asia's growing appetite for dairy products. New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has called it unsustainably high at current levels.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has risen 1.0% over the same period against its counterpart in Australia, which was New Zealand's main trading partner until it was recently overtaken by China.\par \par \uc2 Further fueling the recent rally was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest-rate increases in March and April, which were intended to tame inflation and cool a real-estate market at risk of overheating. The benchmark interest rate now stands at 3.0%, much higher than in other developed economies.\par \par \uc2 The interest-rate differential with neighboring Australia is particularly seen as bullish for the kiwi. On Tuesday, \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its policy rate at a record-low 2.5% for the eighth meeting in a row and signaled it would keep it at that level for some time to stoke an economy struggling with a fading mining boom.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, has said it plans to raise interest rates by around two percentage points in the current tightening cycle, which it expects to last at least two years. Given that plan, any attempts at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the kiwi will have limited success, said ASB Economist Nick Tuffley.\par \par \uc2 Fergus McDonald, head of bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Tyndall Investment Management New Zealand LTD, which has around NZ$3.5 billion under management in New Zealand, also expects the kiwi to remain firm.\par \par \uc2 "If the RBNZ sticks to its guns and puts up interest rates and the rest of the world doesn't, it will continue to support the kiwi," he said.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand policy makers have acted to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  previously. In late 2012 and early 2013 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in nearly four years. The amount, however, was limited and prompted criticism that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had misled markets over the extent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to "talk" the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also may reflect frustration at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued strength in the face of falling prices of dairy products, which account for around a third of exports. Milk prices fell a further 1.1% in the GlobalDairyTrade Auction overnight on Tuesday, bringing the total decline since mid-February to 23%.\par \par \uc2 In any case, David Croy, \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 's head of global markets research for \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly because there is no guarantee such a move would weaken the kiwi significantly.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Mr. Croy interpreted Mr. Wheeler's comments as a warning. They are a "reminder that the economy will start to come under pressure if commodity prices weaken further and the New Zealand dollar doesn't respond," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 07, 2014 04:23 ET (08:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140507ea57001c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
