\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Lower Late After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 07:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading slightly lower late Wednesday after Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Graeme Wheeler said it is overvalued and if it remains high the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could opt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The kiwi gained overnight but took a tumble when Mr. Wheeler told the \uc2 DairyNZ\uc2  Farmers' Forum in Hamilton that if the "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains high in the face of worsening fundamentals, such as a continued weakening in export prices, it would become more opportune for the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell NZ dollars."\par \par \uc2 Also on Wednesday, first-quarter jobs data pointed to softer-than-expected wage inflation, which added to the pressure.\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading, the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8690 compared with US$0.8695 late Tuesday in New Zealand. It was trading at US$0.8742 prior to Mr. Wheeler's speech. It was at A$0.9304 from A$0.9375 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The kiwi is lower, as you would expect with a wage cost report showing very soft wage inflation still and Wheeler's speech, which reminded us the high kiwi will probably translate into a lower interest rate track and also that they are one step closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Westpac\uc2  Bank Senior Strategist, Imre Speizer.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Speizer, however, doesn't expect it to push much below US$0.8650 although "a lot depends on how the U.S. performs overnight." Key for markets will be testimony from Federal Reserve Chairwoman Janet Yellen later in the global trading day, said Mr. Speizer.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 07, 2014 01:37 ET (05:37 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140507ea57000je\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
