\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ Assistant Governor McDermott: New Zealand's Exchange Rate Overvalued\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2013\par 00:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--The historically high New Zealand dollar remains a significant headwind for the country's export sector but keeping interest rates low or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would have little impact, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor John McDermott said in a speech Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The New Zealand dollar is overvalued from the standpoint of its effects on the economy and we would like to see a lower exchange rate," Mr. McDermott told lobby group Federated Farmers.\par \par \uc2 "The bank does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time-to-time. But evidence from the past, here and elsewhere, suggests foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to have a sustained impact in lowering the exchange rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 Daily foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions in \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars "swamp any practical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capacity," as they average around 100 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars (US$82 billion) a day with more than 80% of transactions taking place offshore, Mr. McDermott said.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the solution lies in improved microeconomic policies, in particular those that promote greater competition, Mr. McDermott said. He also noted New Zealand's dependence on foreign funding "means that we have persistently needed interest rates above those in most developed economies," adding to pressure on the New Zealand dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Raising domestic savings relative to our investment needs appears the best way to sustainably lower New Zealand's real interest rates and take the pressure off the real exchange rate," Mr. McDermott said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 21, 2013 18:43 ET (23:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131121e9bl0054f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
