\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-New Zealand central banker's comments boost "overvalued" NZ dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu   \par \uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2013\par 23:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, detail, background)\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Nov 22 (Reuters) - When Reserve Bank of New Zealand Assistant Governor \uc2 John McDermott\uc2  said on Friday the New Zealand dollar was overvalued and he would like to see it weaken, it did exactly the opposite and rose to a session high.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Wellington, McDermott conceded the RBNZ was not inclined to actively weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it prepares to raise interest rates next year, which markets took as little more than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's usual jawboning against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength and drove it higher.\par \par \uc2 McDermott's comments appeared to acknowledge that the RBNZ was unwilling to enter the $4 trillion-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the "kiwi" at the moment, given its limited resources to take on overseas players controlling roughly 90 percent of trade who have been buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its relatively higher yield.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi popped up to a session high of $0.8245 after the speech, as the absence of any signal that the RBNZ would try to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred some buying.\par \par \uc2 McDermott said the New Zealand dollar was at historically high levels due the country's current high terms of trade, particularly booming dairy prices, and relatively strong economic performance.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  believes that, from a long-term perspective, the exchange rate is overvalued," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The high exchange rate is contributing to economic imbalances and the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  would like to see it lower in order to promote more sustainable economic growth."\par \par \uc2 But he added that evidence in \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other countries suggested that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to have a sustained impact on lowering the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the RBNZ will raise rates from a record low 2.5 percent early next year has boosted the kiwi, which hovers in range of a post-float high hit against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket earlier this year after gaining nearly 5 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Ongoing strength in the kiwi has been a headache for RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 , who said last week that he was concerned that a looming rise in interest rates would put upward pressure on the New Zealand dollar.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ's tone on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength has been tempered compared with a speech by Reserve Bank of Australia Governor \uc2 Glenn Stevens\uc2 , who on Thursday said he was "open-minded" on whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the high Australian dollar, stepping up his rhetoric after long complaining of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, in this episode so far, the bank has not been convinced that large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly passed the test of effectiveness versus cost. But that doesn't mean we will always eschew \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Stevens told the Australian Business Economists' annual dinner.\par \par \uc2 ANZ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sam Tuck said the RBA was taking a stronger position against the "Aussie" as it approaches the end of its monetary easing cycle -- which has done little to depreciate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- while the RBNZ is widely expected to enter a monetary tightening cycle next year.\par \par \uc2 "The RBA can afford to be a bit more activist against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because there's no danger in the short term of their actions boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Tuck said.\par \par \uc2 "The RBNZ has to be a little bit more pragmatic because they have to justify why strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't going to impede them from achieving their primary goal, which is to ensure price stability and make sure house price and construction inflation doesn't spill into the broader economy."\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has said it expects to begin raising interest rates, which have been at a record low 2.5 percent since April 2011, sometime in 2014 to counter growing inflation pressures from a stronger economy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters overwhelmingly expect the tightening cycle to start in March next year, with markets pricing in nearly 100 basis points tightening in a year's time .\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Eric Meijer)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/RBNZ (UPDATE 1) | ABX | AUF | ABN | D | M | ND | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131121e9bl001m0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
