\par\par \b \uc2 Australia & NZ dlrs bounce, data and RBNZ a big help\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2013\par 22:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Aussie up 2 pct so far in October, housing data surprisingly strong\par \par \uc2 * Kiwi off 6-wk lows after RBNZ signals rate rises next year\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says high NZD gives it more flexibility on when to hike\par \par \uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu and Cecile Lefort\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar bounced on Thursday after surprisingly strong housing data showed record-low interest rates were helping the economy gain traction, lessening the need for further easing.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar also got a lift after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  disappointed doves by reiterating that higher rates would likely be needed next year.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie hopped up half a U.S. cent to $0.9504 as government data showed approvals to build new homes surged 14.4 percent in September, far above forecasts.\par \par \uc2 The number of approvals was the highest since March 2010 while their dollar value was the highest on record, a comfort to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  (RBA) which has been counting on home construction to underpin growth as mining cools.\par \par \uc2 "Housing is taking the baton from mining and will drive the economy over the next year," said \uc2 Craig James\uc2 , chief economist at CommSec.\par \par \uc2 "Multiplier effects from housing on the economy are significant, meaning many sectors will share in the gains of the building boom," he added. "The RBA is reluctant to cut rates again given the signs of firmer economic activity."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its November policy meeting next week and is thought almost certain to keep rates at 2.5 percent. Interbank futures <0#YIB:> imply only a 36 percent probability of any further cuts in rates.\par \par \uc2 Australian government bond futures were hard hit with the three-year bond contract down 9 ticks at 96.950 and off a one-month peak. The 10-year contract lost 6.5 ticks to 96.005, leading to a bearish flattening of the yield curve.\par \par \uc2 Still the strength of the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a drag on trade-sensitive sectors and argued for the RBA keeping a mild easing bias for now.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie had climbed 5 cents since late August to reach a five-month peak last week. Immediate support is seen at $0.9441, with resistance at $0.9520, the 50 percent retracement of the $0.9280-$0.9758 move.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar bounced off lows after the RBNZ reiterated its outlook for interest rate rises next year while protests against the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not as aggressive as some had expected.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi rose to $0.8257, from a six-week trough of $0.8193. It was still on track to show a loss of 0.5 percent for the month, having skidded 2-1/2 cents in little over a week.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi's bounce came after RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said that rates would rise in 2014 as economic growth picks up.\par \par \uc2 Yet, he also added that the ongoing strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would give him more flexibility regarding the timing and size of monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 Some traders had been expecting Wheeler to take a more aggressive stance against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, and as a result short positions were squeezed.\par \par \uc2 "There was quite a lot of anticipation that the (RBNZ) statement would be softer ... it appears that the market was overly anticipating a dovish statement," said Nick Tuffley, chief economist at \uc2 ASB Bank\uc2  in Auckland.\par \par \uc2 "The bounce back has been driven by the reinforcement that the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  would prefer the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be lower but it's not trying to actively jawbone it down, and that it's very unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bond prices slid, sending yields as much as 7 basis points higher. (Editing by \uc2 Simon Cameron-Moore\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 1) | AUF | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ND | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131102e9au00094\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
