\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Gains Vs Greenback On Broad U.S. Dollar Weakness\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 901 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2013\par 06:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--The New Zealand dollar was trading higher against the U.S. dollar late Monday amid broad weakness in the U.S. dollar and ongoing demand for the Kiwi against the backdrop of a buoyant local economy.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar is in a "sweet spot" for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength at the moment, \uc2 Bank of New Zealand\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mike Jones said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is "suffering from back-peddling Fed tapering expectations and falling bond yields," he said, while risk appetite is "surging anew" and there is the possibility that "the tailwinds may well carry the Kiwi back up towards April's US$0.8630 highs."\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8486 versus US$0.8458 late Friday. It was at A$0.8785 versus A$0.8792.\par \par \uc2 Tim Kelleher, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  institutional sales at ASB Bank, said the New Zealand dollar may underperform against the Australia dollar this week as local traders worry that "the RBNZ might start poking its nose in." The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed earlier this year it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in an effort to bring down what it saw as a strong New Zealand dollar.\par \par \uc2 Local economic data released during the session continued to support the New Zealand dollar. Statistics New Zealand said the country gained a net 2,740 migrants in September in seasonally adjusted terms, while \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  data showed credit card billings rose 5.2% on the year in the same month.\par \par \uc2 "Another very strong month for net migration can be put down to the rapid slowdown in the number of New Zealanders leaving for Australia," ASB economist Daniel Smith said.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, the key data release locally this week is Thursday's overseas merchandise trade figures for September. A Wall Street Journal poll of 10 economists expects a trade deficit of NZ$800 million.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 22 Oct 2013 01:03 EDT  New Zealand Dollar Down Late as Investors Focus on US Jobs Data\par \par \uc2 By Lucy Craymer\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--The New Zealand dollar is lower late Tuesday, with the pending release of September U.S. non-farm payrolls data in focus.\par \par \uc2 The data had been due for release earlier in the month but was delayed due to the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  shutdown. Analysts expect to see 180,000 jobs added. A reading above 200,000 would send the U.S. dollar higher, said \uc2 Western Union\uc2  Business Solutions Corporate Dealing Manager Chris Hunter.\par \par \uc2 In late Wellington trading, the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8445 versus US$0.8486 late Monday. It was at A$0.8754 versus A$0.8785.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Hunter added that the market was looking for information about the state of the U.S. economy, with the outlook of the Federal Reserve bond-buying program remaining a focus for markets.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar also pulled back against the Australian dollar. Expectations that the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  will raise the cash rate in March have eased. Analysts have said that strength in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offset inflation pressure and new macroprudential tools may reduce concerns over an Auckland housing-market bubble.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 22 Oct 2013 23:46 EDT  New Zealand Dollar Mixed Late; Offshore Data Dominate\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Lucy Craymer \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AUCKLAND, New Zealand--The New Zealand dollar is mixed late Wednesday, sidelined in favor of events offshore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Kiwi opened the local session higher against the U.S. dollar following an overnight rally "after the U.S. payrolls report disappointed the market, causing a sharp decline in U.S. interest rates and the U.S. dollar," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy created 148,000 jobs in September, the Labor Department said Tuesday. That fell short of economists' expectations for 180,000 jobs, although the unemployment rate ticked lower, to 7.2% from 7.3% the previous month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, some of the Kiwi's gains were pared as the New Zealand dollar was sold off in favor of the Australian dollar following higher-than-expected inflation data out of that country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian consumer prices rose 1.2% in the third quarter from the second and were up 2.2% from a year earlier, led by sharp rises in fuel and travel costs, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australian Bureau of Statistics\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. Economists had expected the consumer price index to rise 0.8% on the quarter and 1.8% on the year. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  targets an inflation rate of between 2% and 3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In late Wellington trading, the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.8475 versus US$0.8445 late Tuesday. It was at A$0.8705 versus A$0.8754.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The focus locally now turns to overseas merchandise trade data due Thursday morning. The median in a Wall Street Journal poll of 10 economists is for a trade deficit of NZ$800 million in September, while the annual deficit is expected to edge wider to NZ$2.1 billion from NZ$2.06 billion as of Aug. 31.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 22, 2013 23:46 ET (03:46 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131021e9al000ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
