\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-NZ's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  shifts to buying kiwi in May\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2013\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst view on c.bank's possible strategy)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys NZ dollar after 3 months of selling\par \par \uc2 * Analyst sees move as possible profit-taking\par \par \uc2 * NZ dlr down more than 10 pct in past two months\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 27 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  (RBNZ) bought a net NZ$90 million ($70 million) in May, following three months of net selling, in what may have been profit-taking after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent sharp decline.\par \par \uc2 In April, the RBNZ sold a net NZ$256 million, the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in five years, after the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, the bank's preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure, hit its highest against a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the kiwi was floated in 1985.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi has fallen more than 10 percent since it hit a 20-month high in mid-April against the U.S. dollar. The greenback's recent gains against high yield and emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflect expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will soon start reducing its quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 One analyst said the RBNZ may be thinking that the kiwi had fallen as far as it was going to in the near term.\par \par \uc2 "Did they buy back what they sold in the previous month and made a profit? That's entirely plausible," said \uc2 Westpac\uc2  senior strategist Imre Speizer.\par \par \uc2 The May purchase of New Zealand dollars was the first since January, and the most since March 2011, when the bank bought a net NZ$525 million.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the RBNZ said the kiwi dollar was still overvalued despite its recent fall.\par \par \uc2 RBNZ Governor Graham Wheeler has said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be more active in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and that it is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  where it thinks it has a good chance of influencing the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 However, he has also said that, at best, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will work at the margins and look to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar last traded at $0.7816, up about 0.5 percent on the day as the U.S. dollar softened.   ($1=NZ$1.28)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/RBNZ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | ND | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130627e96r00036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
