\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ Gov. says will  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  again if necessary\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2013\par 23:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 13 (Reuters) - Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  on Thursday said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again if the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strengthened further.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Wheeler repeated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to sell the New Zealand dollar if the opportunity arose.\par \par \uc2 However, he said that the RBNZ would not try to offset any strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rise in the New Zealand dollar was driven by strong capital flows.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ sold a net NZ$256 million ($203.96 million) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April, when the trade-weighted New Zealand dollar rose to a post-float high.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates at a record low 2.5 percent for the 18th straight month on Thursday as widely expected.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 1.2552 New Zealand dollars) (Reporting by Naomi Tajitsu)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/WHEELER (URGENT) | ABN | D | M | ND | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130612e96c0010t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
