\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  Draws Criticism\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2013\par 08:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold much less of its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings last month than economists had been expecting, prompting charges it misled markets over the extent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to help drive down the soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  forewarned that it had "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April to help ease pressure on the country's exporters grappling with an elevated Kiwi, which has risen about 10% in the past year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The New Zealand dollar dropped nearly a cent against the U.S. dollar on that announcement.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  routinely buys and sells small amounts of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support liquidity, the Reserve Bank's explicit reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first since 2007, leading some economists and strategists to believe the April sell-off would be significantly higher than the 256 million New Zealand dollar (US$208 million) figure subsequently announced Thursday. Some economists had expected a figure of as much as NZ$1 billion.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, Gov. \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if circumstances demanded it, pushing the Kiwi lower by almost half a cent against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Annette Beacher, Singapore-based head of Asia-Pacific research at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 , said the final number for April fell "far short" of expectations.\par \par \uc2 "Does this confirm that all along that it is merely jawboning the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower?" she said. "We question the wisdom of such announcements of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by senior RBNZ staff when the evidence clearly shows a lack of resolve."\par \par \uc2 Alex Sinton, Auckland-based director of institutional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group\uc2 , was also critical.\par \par \uc2 "It was misleading, absolutely, the governor deliberately played it up," he said. "Clearly the amount was insignificant. What will be interesting will be May's numbers."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had no comment on the suggestion its use of the word \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was misleading.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in Australia, \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and parts of Asia have been stepping up moves to deal with an influx of international capital as investors scour the globe looking for higher returns in countries where interest rates remain relatively high following the global financial crisis. The inflows have kept \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Aussie and Kiwi strong, while complicating efforts to manage growth.\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut interest rates to a record low 2.75%--still above the U.S. and much of Europe--and at its monthly policy meetings frequently notes the stubborn strength of the Australian dollar. New Zealand's benchmark cash rate is at 2.5%, where it's been since March 2011 to help the economy recover from a series of devastating earthquakes.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, China is moving to curb bets on the rising yuan, while Thailand this month was looking at ways to deal with the strongest baht since the 1997 Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was in 2007, when it was also seeking to bring down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It sold nearly NZ$1.5 billion in June of that year and about NZ$1.6 billion between February and June 2008.\par \par \uc2 "The timid nature of this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests that the RBNZ doubts its effectiveness and is prepared to only act to counter spikes higher," said Greg Gibbs, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 , who is based in Singapore. "This activity is much below the more aggressive actions undertaken in 2007-08."\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 30, 2013 02:25 ET (06:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130530e95u000tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
