\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ Blog:New Zealand  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seeks Clearing House for Trades\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2013\par 00:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's MoneyBeat blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Lucy Craymer\par \par \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seeking a clearing house to handle its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and other financial trades, bringing it in line with new reforms in the U.S. and Europe which will force much of the global over-the-counter derivatives market to be cleared rather than conducted in private, bilateral trades.\par \par \uc2 It comes as Reserve Bank of New Zealand Gov. Graeme Wheeler admitted earlier this month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by reducing its \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar holdings, and would do so again if needed to contain a soaring local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's dragging on tourism and denting the competitiveness of the nation's agricultural exports.\par \par \uc2 Normally during an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars on the spot market, without using a clearing house. But a clearing house could handle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to balance the outflow after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 Tender documents seen by the Wall Street Journal show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has requested proposals from clearing houses to manage on average a couple of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap, cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basic swap and single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest-rate swap transactions a month valued at about $200 million each.\par \par \uc2 A clearing house acts as a facilitator for two parties that want to trade financial instruments such as stocks, bonds or derivatives, and like an insurer, it may be liable for the value of a trade if one of the parties defaults. A Reserve Bank spokeswoman said adopting a clearing house system would help the bank manage its risks.\par \par \uc2 In December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold nearly 200 million New Zealand dollars (US$161 million) in the most significant sale in nearly four years, official data show. The pace of its sales slowed early this year, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling only NZ$28 million in the first three months of the year combined. The Reserve Bank is due to release foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction data for April later this month and some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have gathered pace again.\par \par \uc2 Parties interested in acting as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's clearing agent have until July 1 to submit a proposal. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  "For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ." \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 29, 2013 18:12 ET (22:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130529e95t00629\par }\page {\par\fs2