\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar falls after RBNZ gov talks  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2013\par 22:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, May 30 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell more than a quarter of a cent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise and would continue to do so if the opportunity arose and it had a good chance of working.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell to a low of $0.8100 from around $0.8130 after the comments, before settling back at around $0.8108.\par \par \uc2 RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  told a business group that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was significantly overvalued but it was fortunate that it had fallen in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank had battled the high exchange rate through holding its cash rate low and by targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are prepared to scale up our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities if we see opportunities to have greater influence," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Gyles Beckford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND/(URGENT) | ABN | D | M | ND | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130601e95t0009q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
