\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-PREVIEW-RBNZ set to lay bare modest, stealthly  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2013\par 21:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBNZ data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due 0300 GMT Thursday\par \par \uc2 * Analysts expect RBNZ sold NZ$300-NZ$350 mln in April to rein in kiwi\par \par \uc2 * Resurgent US dollar takes pressure off kiwi\par \par \uc2 * RBNZ's Wheeler up front on limitations of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, May 29 (Reuters) - Rare \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength last month is likely to have ended as quietly as it began thanks to a subsequent resurgence in the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  will disclose on Thursday the amount of New Zealand or "kiwi" dollars it sold in April, offering the first details of its low-level \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was initially revealed during a parliamentary committee hearing earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Market participants expect the RBNZ offloaded around NZ$300 million to NZ$500 million ($242-404 million) in April. That is much less than the roughly NZ$1.5 billion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold in July 2007, during its last campaign to actively weaken the kiwi.\par \par \uc2 Since April, the kiwi has lost roughly 7 percent against the U.S. dollar, but analysts say the move has been driven by external factors.\par \par \uc2 "The fall in the kiwi since early May has been all about U.S. dollar strength and that's about fears that the Fed's QE will be unwound," said Imre Speizer, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 . "It's got nothing to do with the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  and '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats'."\par \par \uc2 Since taking the helm at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  has expressed his disdain of the kiwi's strength, which has tormented exporters in the agricultural economy.\par \par \uc2 But the kiwi is the 10th most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the $4 trillion global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited firepower. Wheeler said in an early speech as governor that there were "clear limits to what monetary policy and exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do to lower the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar".\par \par \uc2 Market participants say the risk of more kiwi selling is unlikely for now, given that its trade-weighted index has retreated to around 76.5 from a post-float high around 79.4. However, more RBNZ selling may resume if the index hits a new historic high.\par \par \uc2 "A trade-weighted index above 80 would certainly have people speculating about more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling," said a trader in Auckland. ($1 = 1.2369 New Zealand dollars) (Reporting by Naomi Tajitsu; Editing by \uc2 Simon Cameron-Moore\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-RBNZ/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT) | ABN | D | ND | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130601e95t00098\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
