\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Flat in Quiet Trade; Terms of Trade Awaited\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2013\par 08:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar was little changed Tuesday, with markets quiet following a holiday in the U.S. and the U.K. Monday.\par \par \uc2 Western Union\uc2  Business Solutions Corporate Dealing Manager Chris Hunter said markets have been trading sideways, with direction likely to come from the U.K. and the U.S. overnight.\par \par \uc2 At 0426 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading unchanged at US$0.8086, while it was at A$0.8387, slightly lower from Monday when its was trading at A$0.8395.\par \par \uc2 The local focus is on first-quarter terms of trade data, expected Thursday. The median from a Wall Street Journal poll of 10 economists expects terms of trade--or the difference between export revenues and import expenditure--to be up 1.5% from the previous quarter but down 5.6% from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Later Thursday, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  is set to release data on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets, liabilities and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows. The data, often ignored by the market, are now keenly awaited after Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  admitted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but refused to confirm the extent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bonds due April 2015 rose 4.5 basis points to 2.555% while April 2023 bonds were up 3.5 basis points at 3.495%.\par \par \uc2 A local trader said the New Zealand government bond market saw prices fall after a selloff in the Australian market.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com [ 28-05-13 0653GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130528e95s0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
