\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand cenbank governor deploys tactical  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gyles Beckford   \par \uc2 1,027 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2013\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, May 10 (Reuters) - In the global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  arena small player New Zealand probably deployed its last best tactic this week - a strategically timed disclosure.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 , knocked around half a cent off the New Zealand dollar after divulging at a parliamentary committee that it had been active in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The small South Pacific agricultural economy is grappling with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has been driven to near-record levels in part by demand from investors with cheap money chasing New Zealand's comparatively high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The elevated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is helping to contain imported inflation but is undermining exporters.\par \par \uc2 Wheeler's comments revealed few details and he gave no idea whether it was full-blooded selling of the kiwi, of the likes seen in 2007, or more discreet and passive management of reserves, but he conceded that the latest actions were unlikely to have materially changed the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "We could potentially take the tops off rallies," Wheeler told the committee, as he conceded, yet again, that the bank can do little to combat a "significantly overvalued" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That was small comfort for a tradables sector battling a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that hit a 20-month high in mid-April and is in sight of the 28 year post-float high of $0.8842 touched in August 2011.\par \par \uc2 But the reality spelled out to the committee is that minnows, such as New Zealand, suffer the collateral damage from the loose money policies of the U.S. Federal Reserve, \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 , which account for around two-thirds of the word's output.\par \par \uc2 "All those factors ... are pushing down interest rates and by the same token New Zealand is attracting very substantial capital flows that's putting pressure on the exchange rate, so it's a double-edged sword."\par \par \uc2 Analysts see the RBNZ's jawboning as little more than a token effort, given the resources at hand are like a peashooter, as the Finance Minister called it earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 "It's impossible to move a market that turns over around $27 billion per day with a small amount of passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 "," said Sean Keane of Triple-T Consulting.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which is freely tradable, accounts for around 2 percent of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading.\par \par \uc2 BLAME IT ON THE FED\par \par \uc2 So the New Zealand dollar's best bet would seem to lie in major central banks around the world, but most notably the Fed, paring back their money printing policies.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed's QE policies are currently adding around 10 cents onto the fair-value of the kiwi," said \uc2 Bank of New Zealand\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mike Jones in a recent research report, which estimated the fair value at $0.7500 to $0.7900.\par \par \uc2 "So unless you think the Fed is about to halt or reverse QE; New Zealand commodity prices are about to fall off a cliff; or offshore risk appetite is about to dry up, there is little reason to expect the NZD/USD to head substantially lower anytime soon."\par \par \uc2 In such an environment Wheeler can be expected to engage in periodic bouts of jawboning but little else.\par \par \uc2 A little over a month into the job, last October, he made it clear he was not inclined to tilt at \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  windmills, and that controlling inflation was his priority. It's a message he's repeated several times since.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has clear criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including whether it would work, whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was exceptionally high, and whether the market conditions were right and it has a good chance of succeeding.\par \par \uc2 Arguably most of the conditions have been met, with the notable exception of the chances of success, where the waves of cheap money turned loose by the easy monetary policies of the major economies are looking for a high-yielding home.\par \par \uc2 With a housing market that is moving into record territory, an economy growing around 2.5-3 percent a year, inflation seen moving up to the middle of the RBNZ's target band, and elevated prices for key agricultural exports, the bank has all but ruled out cutting its overnight cash rate to lower the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If we reduced the OCR without sound reasons, the exchange rate might drop initially but rise later when the inflationary implications of the rate cut became clear," Wheeler said last year, a point reiterated in subsequent statements.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand's experience is mirrored in neighbouring Australia, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been struggling with a painfully high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its own.\par \par \uc2 It tried some surreptitious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, selling Aussie dollars directly to central banks that wanted them rather than going through markets.\par \par \uc2 But again the amounts were modest and had no discernible impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overall.\par \par \uc2 Even cutting rates has had scant effect with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually rising after reductions in October and December last year. Its frustration with the high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely one reason it chose to cut again this week, taking its cash rate to an all time trough of 2.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 This time the Aussie eased, but only because the U.S. dollar surged against everything.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 47 analysts shows an expectation the kiwi will be $0.8430 until mid-year an $0.8200 in a year's time.\par \par \uc2 The most likely trigger for a fall in the New Zealand dollar is an end to the Federal Reserve's bond buying or a significant shock such as a slump in the global price of dairy products which make up around a quarter of exports, or a marked slowdown in China, the country's biggest export market.\par \par \uc2 In that environment New Zealand, like other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  small fry, has little choice but to grin and bear it, and every so often say or do something that reminds investors that a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "not a one-way bet".\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Wayne Cole in Sydney; Editing by Eric Meijer)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | ND | AUF | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130510e95a000bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
