\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Weaker Late After U.S. Dollar Breaches Y100\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2013\par 08:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--The New Zealand dollar was trading lower late Friday as the U.S. dollar gained across the board after its move above 100 yen.\par \par \uc2 "It [the New Zealand dollar] is coming under a little bit of pressure. The dominant theme in our session has been the rally in USD/JPY to new four-year highs," said \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Sue Trinh. She noted the movement started in the U.S. session after "hawkish commentary" from U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President \uc2 Charles Plosser\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rally "promoted a broader bid toward the U.S. dollar with it strengthening right across the board, and the Kiwi's been a victim of that as well," said Ms. Trinh. Coupled with comments this week about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 , "the Kiwi looks a bit vulnerable."\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.8368 compared with US$0.8457 Thursday, and at A$0.8301 versus A$0.8262.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar tumbled nearly a cent against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after Gov. Wheeler confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and that it would do so again if needed to contain a soaring local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Market participants are now awaiting a speech by Fed Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  later in the global day, "given the big move was in part driven by Plosser's comments," said Ms. Trinh. "If Bernanke echoes those, or dismisses them, it could either see a continuation of this trend or a reversal."\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand April 2015 government bond rose 1 basis point to end at 2.48%, and the April 2023 bond rose 8.5 basis points to 3.35%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com [ 10-05-13 0610GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130510e95a000h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
