\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Strong New Zealand Jobs Figures Muddy Waters For  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2013\par 04:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --New Zealand dollar jumps on better-than-expected jobs data\par \par \uc2 --Employment rate at three-year low\par \par \uc2 --Labor market "much weaker" excluding Canterbury\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Rebecca Howard \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON--New Zealand's unemployment rate has dropped to its lowest level in three years, highlighting the dilemma for the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it juggles improving economic data and a high \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and causing the Kiwi to erase losses made after Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate fell to 6.2% in the first quarter of the year from a revised 6.8% in the fourth quarter, data from Statistics New Zealand showed Thursday. The rate was the lowest since March 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand dollar jumped on the data and remained higher early afternoon, trading at US$0.8464 at 0221 GMT from US$0.8414 prior to the release. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had tumbled nearly a cent Wednesday after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and would do so again if needed to contain a soaring local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Kiwi's strength comes despite interest rates being held at a record low 2.5% since March 2011 as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  looks to support the economy through a tepid recovery in the wake of a series of devastating earthquakes in the South Island's Canterbury region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gains of around 10% in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past year on a trade-weighted index basis have heightened difficulties for companies in the mainly agriculture-exporting nation looking to compete in global markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated rates will remain on hold this year, but has also said the outlook is "finely balanced." On the one hand, data show the economy growing at its fastest pace in three years in the final quarter of 2012, with increasing fears the housing market may be overheating. On the other, inflation remains extremely benign and the high dollar is acting as a significant headwind.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Just how much the latest data will influence thinking at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is open to debate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While acknowledging the data were stronger than expected, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Senior Economist Mark Smith cautioned that the survey tends to be volatile. He noted that "business sentiment surveys point to a continued willingness to take on more staff, but our job ads survey and anecdotes point to marked sector and regional differences, and do not suggest a smooth recovery."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result, he expects the OCR to "remain on hold for a while yet," and is penciling in a first increase for March.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In contrast, Alvin Pontoh, \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  Asia-Pacific Macro Strategist, notes that despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength, "we continue to believe that a sustained improvement in the data combined with a hot housing market will force the RBNZ to lift the OCR rate from the current record low of 2.5%, in December. This is 3-6 months earlier than the consensus expects."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And while Diane Ramsay, industry and labor statistics manager at Statistics New Zealand, called the data a "strong turnaround," the statistics office also noted that part of the improvement was due to the rebuild in earthquake stricken Canterbury.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Excluding Canterbury from the national estimates shows a much weaker labor market, with both the employment rate and labor force participation rate falling over the year," it said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com [ 05-08-13 2246ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130509e9590000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
