\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Gains After Better-than-Expected Jobs Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2013\par 07:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar was trading higher late Thursday after better-than-expected jobs data helped it erase losses made after Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.\par \par \uc2 The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate fell to 6.2% in the first quarter of the year from a revised 6.8% in the fourth quarter, data from Statistics New Zealand showed. The rate was the lowest since March 2010.\par \par \uc2 At 0453 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.8457, versus US$0.8398 late Wednesday, and at A$0.8262 versus A$0.8248. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had tumbled nearly a cent against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and would do so again if needed to contain a soaring local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The jobs data "put paid to the RBNZ's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' effect. But, if the economy is truly on the recovery path and the markets anticipate rate hikes ahead, then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --especially on the modest scale that has probably been undertaken--is not likely to be successful," said \uc2 Robin Clements\uc2 , an economist with \uc2 UBS\uc2  Economics, in a note.\par \par \uc2 The Kiwi also tracked the Australian dollar higher after Australian jobs data was also better than expected. The Aussie jumped after the \uc2 Australian Bureau of Statistics\uc2  reported the jobless rate fell to a seasonally adjusted 5.5% in April from 5.6% in March. Economists had expected the rate to be unchanged.\par \par \uc2 Tim Kelleher, ASB's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Institutional Sales New Zealand, said the Kiwi could gain more overnight on the back of the positive jobs data, although he said "the market will discount some of it due to the volatility of the number."\par \par \uc2 He said the pair has resistance around US$0.8500 to US$0.8515 but was unlikely to push much higher as the market would remain leery after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  April 2015 government bond rose 2 basis points to end at 2.47%, while the April 2023 bond rose 6.5 basis points to 3.265%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com [ 09-05-13 0507GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130509e9590007u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
